item~ function src/work.rs :: WorkStore::publish :: pub fn publish( &self, store: &Store, slug: &str, supplied_key: Option<&str>, changed: Option<String>, ) -> Result<PublishedInfo, WorkError> { :: Commit the slug's working copy through the store's own publish path — the same gate and the same atomic swap as a web release. Refuses when the published bundle has moved past the draft's base version. The commit set is the publishable set: files marked keep-private are held back (they stay in the working copy), so the published bundle never contains them — and because a publish replaces the whole published tree, a file marked after it was live leaves the published surface with this commit. :: direct :: api
item~ function src/work.rs :: WorkStore::write_file :: pub fn write_file( &self, store: &Store, slug: &str, path: &str, content: &[u8], supplied_key: Option<&str>, keep_private: Option<bool>, ) -> Result<WriteInfo, WorkError> { :: Create or replace one file in the slug's working copy, opening the copy first when needed, and persist the draft before returning — a write that answered is a write that survives a restart. `keep_private`, when carried, sets or clears the file's keep-private mark with the same write; when absent, the mark stands as it was. :: direct :: api
item+ function src/work.rs :: WorkingCopy::is_private :: pub fn is_private(&self, path: &str) -> bool { :: Function WorkingCopy::is_private takes &self, path: &str. It gives back bool. :: inferred :: api
item~ function src/work.rs :: diverged :: pub fn diverged(store: &Store, slug: &str, copy: &WorkingCopy) -> bool { :: Does this draft differ from what's published? The three-state word (Drafting / Current / Diverged) rests on this comparison. The comparison is against the publishable set: a file marked keep-private is not a difference from the published bundle — it is deliberately not in it. :: direct :: api
