item~ function src/http.rs :: xml_escape :: pub fn xml_escape(s: &str) -> String { :: XML-escape text for the RSS feed (same five characters as HTML, without the apostrophe form XML parsers also accept). Control characters XML 1.0 forbids outright — everything below U+0020 except tab, line feed, and carriage return — are replaced with U+FFFD: left raw, a single one (a stray bell or vertical tab in a markdown source, say) makes the whole feed not well-formed, and every subscriber's parser refuses it — the same silent death as one unescaped `&`, by another character. :: direct :: api
